WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.930
Even though IT's Pennywise brags about being
everything you're afraid of, there are plenty

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.140
of clowns who may even be scarier than the
extra-dimensional terror monster.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.100
And we're not talking about those kinda-creepy
clowns from Pee-Wee's Big Adventure, or even

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.520
the Insane Clown Posse.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:22.260
There are some very real reasons to develop
a serious case of Bozophobia; here are just

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:22.760
a few.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.260
Sweet Tooth

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:30.220
Needles Kane, better known to gamers as Sweet
Tooth, is a serial psycho clown who drives

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.240
a well-armed ice cream truck in an apocalyptic
demolition derby.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.320
He's been driving that terrible truck since
the first Twisted Metal game in 1995, and

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.400
he's only gotten creepier since.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.620
Over the course of the original Twisted Metal
series, he evolved from a standard psycho

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:50.850
clown with green hair to a flaming, cursed
monster who's forced to carry the fires of

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.040
hell around with him.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:57.180
Sure, the fires of hell are pretty scary,
but the 2012 Twisted Metal reboot made the

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.420
clown even creepier, making him a guy who
tries to slay his entire family after going

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.580
insane with boredom.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:07.000
Sweet Tooth spends years trying to find his
daughter, who escaped the slaying spree, so

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.620
he can finish what he started.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.060
It's just video game fun that causes other
people to get slayed along the way.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:14.660
The Joker

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.700
He's a force of pure chaos, and Batman's greatest
enemy.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.740
The Joker has had various origin stories over
the years and they tend to involve falling

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.640
into a vat of chemicals while trying to escape
Batman, but who he was before that is up in

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.140
the air.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.000
In his original 1951 origin, he was already
a villain known as the Red Hood. 1988's The

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.189
KillingJoke graphic novel elaborated on this
story, making him an aspiring comedian who

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:42.820
had only turned to crime to support his pregnant
wife.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:47.360
But even within that book, this sympathetic
backstory is called into question, with the

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.740
Joker saying that he prefers his past to be
"multiple choice."

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.680
For every new Joker, there's a new origin
story.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.579
The lack of a clear identity is what the Joker
is all about: He's dedicated to the idea that

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:03.279
the world makes no sense, and will merk,
maim, and mutilate anyone who crosses his

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.280
path to illustrate that there are no reasons.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.460
He's not just a mad clown, he's a clown that
embodies madness.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.140
"Haha."

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:16.840
Twisty

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:22.650
Few clowns have ever been as visually frightening
as Twisty, the deranged psycho featured in

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.620
Freak Show, the fourth season of American
Horror Story.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.140
Creator Ryan Murphy has even said that members
of the crew would leave during Twisty's scenes

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.980
because he was just so frightening.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.580
Once a circus clown who loved to entertain
children, Twisty's career was ruined by false

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.820
rumors of pedophilia.

00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:43.079
He failed at offing himself with a shotgun,
but succeeded in blowing off his lower jaw,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.660
thus the half-mask with the terrifying smile.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.860
What's underneath it is even more horrific.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.040
Leaving reality entirely behind, Twisty begins
kidnapping children in a supposed effort to

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.120
save them from their oppressive parents.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:59.579
He's convinced children still love him and
long to be entertained by his antics, even

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.380
as every child who sees him screams and runs
away.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.480
Maybe that horrifying mask was a bad choice.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.340
Madcap

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.840
The best thing about a psycho clown is that
you can usually slay it, but that's not the

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.780
case with Madcap, Marvel's clowniest supervillain.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:20.120
He first appeared in Captain America #307
as a nemesis to the all-American hero and

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.470
his pal Nomad, but he doesn't seem to care
much about superheroes at all, until they

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.760
get in the way of his goal of spreading chaos.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.680
Madcap has two superpowers.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.620
First, he can't be hurt; any injury
he suffers heals almost instantly, and if

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.420
he dies, he comes back to life.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.840
Second, he can make other people behave irrationally
by making eye contact with them, making ordinary

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.480
citizens put themselves in danger, by dancing
through traffic or even leaping off of buildings.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.060
A clown who will slay you is scary, but a
clown who cuts off his own fingers just for

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.640
fun is even scarier.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.560
The Poltergeist clown

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.580
1982's Poltergeist is one of the all-time
greatest haunted house movies.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.840
And like most standard haunted houses, a lot
of the horror early in the film comes from

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.000
inanimate objects moving on their own.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.920
So when young Robbie notices late at night
that a clown doll that was sitting in a chair

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.819
by his bed has suddenly disappeared, that's
already scary.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.480
And then things get really bad.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:24.580
The 2015 Poltergeist remake overdoes its attempt
to one-up this scene, with multiple clown

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:29.580
dolls in a much darker room, but nothing in
that film measures up to the scares of the

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.080
original.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.540
Violator

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.740
Few clowns are actually from hell, but the
Violator is a straight-up demon.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:42.400
He's the main antagonist in Todd McFarlane's
Spawn comics, as well as the 1997 Spawn movie.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.480
"Every time somebody farts a demon gets their
wings.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:47.980
Oops!

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:48.580
Twins."

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:53.260
His entire purpose is to mess with Spawn,
who was given his powers by the forces of

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:53.760
Hell.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:58.020
Since those powers will eventually run out
and force Spawn's return to hell for all eternity,

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.500
the role of Violator is not just to tempt
and corrupt Spawn into doing evil, it's to

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.020
manipulate him into using his powers recklessly.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.380
Violator isn't just a clown — he's
here to shepherd a soul toward eternal damnation,

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.280
and he does it with a grin.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.400
Clown

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:20.100
Perhaps no clown ever created is as terrifying
as the creature at the center of Clown, an

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.920
ancient demon that devours children.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.620
Clown takes over anyone who puts on the cursed
clown costume, which is made from Clown's

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:27.620
own skin and hair.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:32.100
In the film, this happens to Kent, a regular
dad who's just trying to provide last-minute

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.900
entertainment at his son's birthday party.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.720
Once he puts on the suit, he begins transforming
into an inhuman, kid-chomping monster.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:43.760
At first, the horror of Clown comes from Kent's
loss of control as the demon takes over.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.760
But by the end of the film, there's no saving
him, and the horror comes from the rampaging

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.340
monster clown that he's become.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.940
You can be sure of one thing: this is the
scariest clown in movie history.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.160
And there's never been a better advertisement
for Chuck E. Cheese.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:58.840
"Cannonball!"

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.860
"Gross, somebody peed in here."

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:05.900
Thanks for watching!

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.900
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

